      "strengths_deep_dive": [
        "GiveDirectly's strength lies in its lean operational model and commitment to evidence. The charity has <cite id=\"11\">11.4 months of working capital</cite> in reserve, ensuring long-term resilience. Its <cite id=\"12\">Platinum Seal of Transparency from Candid</cite> confirms that it shares comprehensive data on its goals and outcomes. Furthermore, the organization uses a <cite id=\"13\">documented theory of change</cite> to guide its cash delivery, which has been shown to cost approximately <cite id=\"14\">$56.78 per beneficiary</cite> in humanitarian contexts."
      ],
      "summary": "GiveDirectly is a humanitarian organization that provides unconditional cash transfers to people living in extreme poverty. Since its <cite id=\"1\">founding in 2009</cite>, the charity has focused on a direct service model that empowers recipients to prioritize their own needs. In FY2024, the organization reported <cite id=\"2\">total revenue of $140,343,295</cite> to support its operations across Africa and the United States. The charity maintains a <cite id=\"3\">94/100 overall score from Charity Navigator</cite>, reflecting its commitment to financial health and transparency. Its operations are highly efficient, with a <cite id=\"4\">program expense ratio of 91.8%</cite> in FY2024. This means the vast majority of funds go directly to those in need rather than administrative costs. The organization has <cite id=\"5\">delivered cash to over 2 million beneficiaries</cite> to date. By establishing cash as a benchmark for aid, GiveDirectly aims to reshape the social sector and end extreme poverty. The charity operates in several countries, including <cite id=\"7\">Kenya, Rwanda, Liberia, and Malawi</cite>.",
